</span></span><button class="info"
            type="button"
            popovertarget="p98"
            aria-label="Credit">i</button><span id="p98" popover class="pop">Koyos · Public domain</span>
                    <a class="edit"
       href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q30#P138"
       aria-label="Edit"><svg aria-hidden="true" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="m15.4.4 4.2 4.2-3.2 3.2-4.2-4.2zM10.8 5 15 9.2l-8.6 8.6-4.5 1.5-1.2-1.2 1.5-4.5z"/></svg></a>
                </span><img class="pic k-photo"
     style="--a:0.7873"
     src="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/America%20sattelite.jpg?width=330"
     alt=""
     loading="lazy">
        </div></dl></div><dl class="sheet" data-slot="sheet"><div class="row r-value"><dt class="i-puzzle">IPA transcription</dt>
<dd><span class="v">ˈmeɪɹ.ɹɪkə <span class="note quals"><a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1860">English</a> · <a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7976">American English</a> · <a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q120768597">comedic pronunciation</a></span>
        <a class="edit"
       href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q30#P898"
       aria-label="Edit"><svg aria-hidden="true" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="m15.4.4 4.2 4.2-3.2 3.2-4.2-4.2zM10.8 5 15 9.2l-8.6 8.6-4.5 1.5-1.2-1.2 1.5-4.5z"/></svg></a>
    </span><span class="v">ʉːɛˈsɑː <span class="note quals"><a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q9043">Norwegian</a></span>
        <a class="edit"
       href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q30#P898"
       aria-label="Edit"><svg aria-hidden="true" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="m15.4.4 4.2 4.2-3.2 3.2-4.2-4.2zM10.8 5 15 9.2l-8.6 8.6-4.5 1.5-1.2-1.2 1.5-4.5z"/></svg></a>
    </span></dd>
<span class="tools"></span>
</div></dl><div class="prose-slot" lang="en"><p>Documented use of the phrase &quot;United States of America&quot; dates back to January 2, 1776. On that day, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephen_Moylan">Stephen Moylan</a>, a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Continental_Army">Continental Army</a> aide to General <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Washington">George Washington</a>, wrote a letter to <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Reed_(politician)">Joseph Reed</a>, Washington's <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aide-de-camp">aide-de-camp</a>, seeking to go &quot;with full and ample powers from the United States of America to Spain&quot; to seek assistance in the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Revolutionary_War">Revolutionary War</a> effort.<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-4"
        aria-label="Note 4">4</button></sup><sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-5"
        aria-label="Note 5">5</button></sup> The first known public usage is an <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anonymous_work">anonymous essay</a> published in the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Williamsburg,_Virginia">Williamsburg</a> newspaper <i><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Virginia_Gazette">The Virginia Gazette</a></i> on April 6, 1776.<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-4"
        aria-label="Note 4">4</button></sup> Sometime on or after June 11, 1776, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Jefferson">Thomas Jefferson</a> wrote &quot;United States of America&quot; in a rough draft of the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Declaration_of_Independence">Declaration of Independence</a>,<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-4"
        aria-label="Note 4">4</button></sup> which was adopted by the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Continental_Congress">Second Continental Congress</a> on July 4, 1776.<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-6"
        aria-label="Note 6">6</button></sup></p><a class="read" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States#Etymology">Etymology ↗</a></div></section>
