       aria-label="Edit"><svg aria-hidden="true" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="m15.4.4 4.2 4.2-3.2 3.2-4.2-4.2zM10.8 5 15 9.2l-8.6 8.6-4.5 1.5-1.2-1.2 1.5-4.5z"/></svg></a></span>
</div></dl><div class="prose-slot" lang="en"><p>The <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Census_Bureau">U.S. Census Bureau</a> reported 331,449,281 residents on April 1, 2020,<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-10"
        aria-label="Note 10">10</button></sup><sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-11"
        aria-label="Note 11">11</button></sup> making the United States the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_and_dependencies_by_population">third-most-populous country</a> in the world, after India and China.<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-12"
        aria-label="Note 12">12</button></sup> The Census Bureau's official 2025 population estimate was 341,784,857, an increase of 3.1% since the 2020 census.<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-13"
        aria-label="Note 13">13</button></sup> According to the Bureau's <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._and_World_Population_Clock">U.S. Population Clock</a>, on July 1, 2024, the U.S. population had a net gain of one person every 16 seconds, or about 5400 people per day.<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-14"
        aria-label="Note 14">14</button></sup> In 2023, 51% of Americans age 15 and over were married, 6% were <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Widowed">widowed</a>, 10% were divorced, and 34% had never been married.<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-15"
        aria-label="Note 15">15</button></sup> In 2023, the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Total_fertility_rate">total fertility rate</a> for the U.S. stood at 1.6 children per woman,<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-16"
        aria-label="Note 16">16</button></sup> and, at 23%, it had the world's highest rate of children living in <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Single_parents_in_the_United_States">single-parent</a> households in 2019.<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-17"
        aria-label="Note 17">17</button></sup> Most Americans live in the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suburb">suburbs</a> of major metropolitan areas.</p><a class="read" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States#Demographics">Demographics ↗</a></div><div class="topic-articles"><div class="topic-article">
    <div class="body">
        <p class="source"><img src="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Wikipedia-logo-v2.svg?width=60" alt="" width="18"> en.wikipedia.org</p>
