    <button class="info"
            type="button"
            popovertarget="p164"
            aria-label="Description">i</button><span id="p164" popover class="pop">portion of a workforce population that is not employed</span></dt>
<dd><data value="6.7" data-f="number">6.7</data> <span class="note">percent</span> <span class="note quals">2013</span>
                <span class="gauge g-proportion" style="--at: 0.067"><span class="track" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span></span></dd>
<span class="tools">
        <span class="prov-none" title="—"></span>
        <a class="edit"
       href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q30#P1198"
       aria-label="Edit"><svg aria-hidden="true" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="m15.4.4 4.2 4.2-3.2 3.2-4.2-4.2zM10.8 5 15 9.2l-8.6 8.6-4.5 1.5-1.2-1.2 1.5-4.5z"/></svg></a></span>
</div></dl><div class="prose-slot" lang="en"><p>The U.S. has a highly developed <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mixed_economy">mixed economy</a><sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-18"
        aria-label="Note 18">18</button></sup> that has been the world's largest nominally <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_largest_historical_GDP">since about 1890</a>.<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-19"
        aria-label="Note 19">19</button></sup> Its 2024 <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gross_domestic_product">gross domestic product</a> (GDP)<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-20"
        aria-label="Note 20">20</button></sup> of more than $29 trillion<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-21"
        aria-label="Note 21">21</button></sup> constituted over 25% of nominal <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gross_world_product">global economic output</a>, or 15% at <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purchasing_power_parity">purchasing power parity</a> (PPP). The country ranks <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_(nominal)">first in the world by nominal GDP</a>,<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-22"
        aria-label="Note 22">22</button></sup> <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_(PPP)">second when adjusted for purchasing power parities</a> (PPP),<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-23"
