</div>
    </div><dl class="sheet" data-slot="sheet"><div class="row r-value"><dt class="i-calendar">inception</dt>
<dd><span class="v"><time datetime="1784-05-12"
      data-p="11">1784-05-12</time> <span class="note quals"><a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q217450">Treaty of Paris (1783)</a> · <a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q60021702">independence recognized by country from which it separated</a></span>
        <a class="edit"
       href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q30#P571"
       aria-label="Edit"><svg aria-hidden="true" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="m15.4.4 4.2 4.2-3.2 3.2-4.2-4.2zM10.8 5 15 9.2l-8.6 8.6-4.5 1.5-1.2-1.2 1.5-4.5z"/></svg></a>
    </span><span class="v"><time datetime="1776-07-04"
      data-p="11">1776-07-04</time> <span class="note quals"><a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q127912">United States Declaration of Independence</a> · <a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1464916">declaration of independence</a></span>
        <a class="edit"
       href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q30#P571"
       aria-label="Edit"><svg aria-hidden="true" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="m15.4.4 4.2 4.2-3.2 3.2-4.2-4.2zM10.8 5 15 9.2l-8.6 8.6-4.5 1.5-1.2-1.2 1.5-4.5z"/></svg></a>
    </span></dd>
<span class="tools"></span>
</div></dl><div class="prose-slot" lang="en"><p>The <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paleo-Indians">first inhabitants of North America</a> migrated from <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siberia">Siberia</a> at least 15,000 years ago, either across the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bering_land_bridge">Bering land bridge</a> or along the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coastal_migration_(Americas)">now-submerged Ice Age coastline</a>.<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-41"
        aria-label="Note 41">41</button></sup><sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-42"
        aria-label="Note 42">42</button></sup> The <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clovis_culture">Clovis culture</a>, which appeared around 11,000 BCE in North America, is believed to be the first widespread culture in the Americas.<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-43"
        aria-label="Note 43">43</button></sup><sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-44"
        aria-label="Note 44">44</button></sup> Over time, Indigenous North American cultures grew increasingly sophisticated, and some, such as the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mississippian_culture">Mississippian culture</a>, developed <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_Agricultural_Complex">agriculture</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southeastern_Ceremonial_Complex">architecture</a>, and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Complex_societies">complex societies</a>.<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-45"
        aria-label="Note 45">45</button></sup> In the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Native_Americans_in_the_United_States">post-archaic period</a>, the Mississippian cultures were located in the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midwestern_United_States">midwestern</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_United_States">eastern</a>, and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southern_United_States">southern</a> regions, and the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algonquian_peoples">Algonquian</a> in the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Lakes_region">Great Lakes region</a> and along the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Coast_of_the_United_States">Eastern Seaboard</a>, while the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hohokam_culture">Hohokam culture</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancestral_Puebloans">Ancestral Puebloans</a> inhabited  <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Southwest">the Southwest</a>.<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-46"
        aria-label="Note 46">46</button></sup> <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Population_history_of_the_Indigenous_peoples_of_the_Americas">Native population estimates</a> of what is now the United States before the arrival of European colonizers range from around 500,000<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-47"
        aria-label="Note 47">47</button></sup><sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-48"
        aria-label="Note 48">48</button></sup> to nearly 10 million.<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-48"
        aria-label="Note 48">48</button></sup><sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-49"
        aria-label="Note 49">49</button></sup> In 2024, an estimated 3.43 million people in the United States identified as <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_peoples_of_the_Americas">American Indian</a> or <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alaska_Natives">Alaska Native</a> alone (thus, identifying with no other racial category) and represented approximately 1% of the U.S. population.<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-50"
        aria-label="Note 50">50</button></sup> An additional 5.68 million people identified as American Indian or Alaska Native in combination with one or more other races, bringing the total of those identifying as American Indian or Alaska Native to approximately 9.11 million.<sup class="ref"><button type="button"
        popovertarget="note-51"
        aria-label="Note 51">51</button></sup></p><a class="read" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States#History">History ↗</a></div><div class="topic-articles"><div class="topic-article">
    <div class="body">
        <p class="source"><img src="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Wikipedia-logo-v2.svg?width=60" alt="" width="18"> en.wikipedia.org</p>
        <a class="title" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_the_United_States" lang="en">History of the United States</a><p class="desc">occurrences and people in the USA throughout history</p></div><img class="pic k-photo"
     style="--a:1.6073"
     src="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/USA%20territorial%20growth.gif?width=330"
     alt=""
     loading="lazy"><span class="tools"><button class="info"
            type="button"
            popovertarget="p236"
            aria-label="Credit">i</button><span id="p236" popover class="pop">Original:  United States Geological Survey (USGS)
Derivative work:  Roke~commonswiki · Public domain</span></span></div></div></section>
